# BUGS

Only hubs and HID's boot keyboards and mice are driven: no mass storage, audio or network devices, nor a keyboard or mouse whose reports need its report descriptor read, nor isochronous or bulk endpoints at all.
A device's first configuration is the one used.
A multi-TT hub runs with one transaction translator.
Memory a device was given goes back to the driver when it leaves, not to the system.
A platform device that firmware puts behind no IOMMU, as the CIX Sky1's controllers are, DMAs straight to memory: devmgr gives it the stub's BTI, and IORT's named components don't yet put one behind an IOMMU.
